# Text files are stored and checked out with LF line endings on every platform,
# so the bytes a Linux CI runner reads are the bytes a Windows editor wrote.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.ttl    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.jsonld text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.xml    text eol=lf
*.xsd    text eol=lf
*.csv    text eol=lf
*.sparql text eol=lf
*.rq     text eol=lf

# Nothing here is a verbatim copy held to a recorded digest, so this file has no
# section protecting one from normalisation. An adapter package does need such a
# section: docs/fixtures-and-provenance.md says why, and the pilot adapter's
# .gitattributes is the worked example.
